'''Clandestine chemistry''' refers to [[chemistry]] performed in secret, typically to avoid [[Law enforcement|regulatory attention]].  

Most clandestine chemistry supplies the [[illegal drug trade]], both historically and today.  Larger labs are run by [[organized crime]], which then distributes product on the [[black market]]. Smaller labs can be run by individual [[Chemist|chemists]].  

However, not all clandestine chemistry manufactures illegal drugs.  [[Home chemistry|Hobbyist chemists]] may work clandestinely on projects that would be legal if overt, in order to skimp on [[Records management|records]], [[Insurance premium|insurance premia]], or [[Process safety|safety controls]].

